---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import Link from "../../components/Link.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import unity_splash from "../../img/unity/unity-splash.jpg"
import unity_hub from "../../img/unity/unity-hub.jpg"
import unity_projects from "../../img/unity/unity-projects.jpg"
import scene_select from "../../img/unity/scene-select.jpg"
import object_basics from "../../img/unity/object-basics.jpg"
import gitignore from "../../img/unity/gitignore.jpg"
import changes from "../../img/unity/changes.jpg"
import choose_vsc from "../../img/unity/choose-vsc.jpg"
import new_script from "../../img/unity/new-script.jpg"
import two_cubes from "../../img/unity/two-cubes.jpg"
import cs_dev_kit from "../../img/unity/cs-dev-kit.png"
import frame from "../../img/unity/frame.png"
---
<Slide t1="Unity Start">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ unity_splash }
            alt="Unity Splash Image"
            height="375"
            width="375" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Setup">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li>Install: Unity Hub (<Link href="https://unity.com/download" />)</li>
        <li>Install choice of engine from there (currently: <code>6000.0.41f1</code>)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ unity_hub }
            alt="Unity Hub"
            height="400"
            width="650" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Projects">
    <ul>
        <li>Create and open projects from the hub</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ unity_projects }
            alt="Unity Projects"
            height="500"
            width="700" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Setup">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Avoid cloud services, Unity Cloud, Unity Version Control, ...
            (for source control we can use GitHub)
        </li>
        <li class="fragment">For now, our projects are <em>3D (Built-In Render Pipeline)</em></li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Project Basics">
    <ul>
        <li>Everything lives in a <em>scene</em></li>
        <li>Add objects by right-clicking here:</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ scene_select }
            alt="Scene Select"
            height="500"
            width="500" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Object Basics">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">To start, we can experiment
            with object position, rotation and size:</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="fragment flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ object_basics }
            alt="Object Basics"
            height="500"
            width="500" />
    </div>

    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">The camera is also an object:
            important to move and rotate it correctly</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Warm-up Exercise">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ frame }
            alt="Frame"
            height="500"
            width="800" />
    </div>

</Slide>

<Slide t2="Aside: Tools (and GitHub)">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Unity Engine via Unity Hub</li>
        <li class="fragment">GitHub Desktop application</li>
        <li class="fragment">GitHub Enterprise (for creating and managing repos)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="Source Control" t2="Optional (For Now)">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Making backups</li>
        <li class="fragment">Seeing the history of changes</li>
        <li class="fragment">Allowing rollback</li>
        <li class="fragment">Allowing collaboration</li>

        <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Between developers</li>
            <li class="fragment">Across machines</li>
        </ul>

        <li class="fragment">Allowing branches (speculative development, snagging)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="GitHub">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">Referring <!-- .element: class="fragment" --> to this video
            (<Link href="https://youtu.be/qpXxcvS-g3g" />)&mdash;though it's old</li>
        <li class="fragment">Create brand new repository on GitHub:</li>

        <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Create <code>README</code> file</li>
            <li class="fragment">Choose <code>.gitignore</code> template: <em>Unity</em></li>
        </ul>

        <li class="fragment">Check out the repo in GitHub Desktop, Visual Studio Code, ...</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Repo Preparation">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li>Edit <code>.gitignore</code> in the editor of your choice (Visual Studio Code
            seems to work well: <em>Open Folder</em>)</li>
        <li>Remove all the leading "<code>/</code>" characters in paths</li>
        <li>(or replace them with "<code>/*/</code>", if your projects are all at top level)</li>
        <li>Check project preferences (<em>Project Settings</em> &#x21E8; <em>Editor</em>):</li>

        <ul>
            <li><em>Version Control</em> &#x21E8; <em>Visible Meta Files</em></li>
            <li><em>Asset Serialization</em> &#x21E8; <em>Mode</em> &#x21E8; <em>Force Text</em></li>
        </ul>

        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Diffs">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ gitignore }
            alt="GirIgnore Changes"
            height="500"
            width="400" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Unity Projects in Subfolders">
    <ul>
        <li>Save complete Unity folders inside the repo folder</li>
        <li>For each new Unity project, there should be a few dozen files</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Changes">
    <p class="text-sm-1">Should just be a few dozen (not 1000's)</p>
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ changes }
            alt="Changes"
            height="500"
            width="300" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Unity Script Basics">
    <div class="fragment">
        <p class="text-sm-2">Set your editor preferences:</p>

        <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ choose_vsc }
                alt="Choose VSC"
                height="300"
                width="600" />
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fragment">
        <p class="text-sm-2">C# support in VS Code:</p>

        <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ cs_dev_kit }
                alt="C# Dev Kit"
                height="300"
                width="600" />
        </div>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Create Script">
    <div class="fragment">
        <ul class="text-sm-2">
            <li>Add a new script to an existing Game Object:</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ new_script }
                alt="New Script"
                height="300"
                width="250" />
        </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-2">
        <li class="fragment">This script will have methods called <code>Start</code>
            (called on scene launch) and <code>Update</code>
            (called every frame, with variable timing)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="First Script">
    <CodeBlock lang="csharp" height="450px" lines="*|9-10">
        { `
using System.Collections;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

public class MyFirstScript : MonoBehaviour
{
    // Start is called before the first frame update
    void Start() {
        Renderer renderer = GetComponent<Renderer>();
        renderer.material.color = Color.red;
    }

    // Update is called once per frame
    void Update() {
    }
}
        `.trim() }
    </CodeBlock>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Simple Steps">
    <ul>
        <li>Get the <code>Renderer</code> component from the current game object</li>
        <li>Set the colour of its material</li>
        <li>Do this once on <code>Start</code> (for now)</li>   
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Quiz (Rotation and Colour)">
    <ul class="text-sm-2">
        <li>Reproduce this, using two cubes:</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ two_cubes }
            alt="Two Cubes"
            height="300"
            width="550" />
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-2">
        <li>Think about the rotations as well as as the colours</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>
